WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.131 --> 00:00:04.497
- [Mark] All right, Elizabeth.

00:00:04.497 --> 00:00:06.349
Elizabeth, you grew up in Tulsa,

00:00:06.349 --> 00:00:07.192
you just told me?

00:00:07.192 --> 00:00:10.234
- [Elizabeth] Yeah, Tulsa, Oklahoma.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.957
- [Mark] And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:13.477
You had both of your parents growing up?

00:00:13.477 --> 00:00:14.634
- [Elizabeth] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:15.719
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:16.750
- [Elizabeth] How was your what?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.867
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:20.125
- Childhood, okay, very well.

00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:22.525
Something like "Little
House on the Prairie".

00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:23.358
I don't know.

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:24.191
- [Mark] Really?

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:26.143
- Yeah, it was something like that.

00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:26.976
- [Mark] That's nice.

00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:28.578
- Back then.

00:00:28.578 --> 00:00:32.328
- [Mark] And you grew
up with other siblings?

00:00:33.318 --> 00:00:34.881
- Yeah, Katie,

00:00:34.881 --> 00:00:37.214
Lizzie and Stacy and Tracey.

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:41.194
That's all, as far as I remember.

00:00:41.194 --> 00:00:42.733
- [Mark] You left home at what age?

00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:43.983
- Oh, about 18.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:45.927
- [Mark] After high school?

00:00:45.927 --> 00:00:46.760
- Yeah.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.730
- [Mark] And where'd you go?

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.703
- Oh, just went on and went
to school or something.

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:55.267
You know Calhoun high
school, further past that.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.410
- [Mark] Oh, in California?
- Yeah.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.478
- [Mark] So you guys moved to California?

00:00:57.478 --> 00:00:59.505
- Yeah, but I never went to college.

00:00:59.505 --> 00:01:00.505
No, not yet.

00:01:02.185 --> 00:01:03.062
Didn't want to do that.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.653
- [Mark] Did you have
kids? Do you have children?

00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:06.247
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.247 --> 00:01:07.197
- [Mark] How many kids?
- Six kids.

00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:09.048
- [Mark] Six kids?
- Yeah.

00:01:09.048 --> 00:01:09.988
- [Mark] And you raised them?

00:01:09.988 --> 00:01:12.546
- Yeah, they're all fine.

00:01:12.546 --> 00:01:13.459
They're beautiful.

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:17.276
And they're healthy and they're happy.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.026
They never complained

00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:21.899
and never complained or anything.

00:01:21.899 --> 00:01:23.638
And that's the way they were.

00:01:23.638 --> 00:01:24.909
- [Mark] You're living on the street here

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:26.311
in downtown LA.

00:01:26.311 --> 00:01:28.867
- This is the city of Los An- yeah.

00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:30.220
- [Mark] And did you live in a tent

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.256
or where are you staying?

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:32.089
- Oh, wherever.

00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:35.491
With friends and family
and things like that.

00:01:35.491 --> 00:01:38.046
And then I go over there

00:01:38.046 --> 00:01:40.044
and then I make a living

00:01:40.044 --> 00:01:41.958
and clean up or do jobs.

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.094
- [Mark] How do you make money?

00:01:43.094 --> 00:01:45.511
- Odd jobs or something and,

00:01:47.614 --> 00:01:50.419
vacuum and clean these kinds of things

00:01:50.419 --> 00:01:52.617
and just wasn't sure what it was.

00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:54.367
Good lessons to pass.

00:01:57.135 --> 00:02:00.885
And things like that
are good for your brain.

00:02:02.004 --> 00:02:04.143
Jogging and exercise every day

00:02:04.143 --> 00:02:05.834
but when I wake up in the morning

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.697
the main thing is I look the same.

00:02:08.697 --> 00:02:11.061
You're ever out there, you know.

00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:13.272
- [Mark] Do you still have-
- My aunt probably

00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:16.210
put that when she was
a nurse or something.

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:17.337
'Cause she looks like that.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.155
She had beautiful eyes.

00:02:19.155 --> 00:02:20.986
- [Mark] Do you still have
contact with your kids?

00:02:20.986 --> 00:02:21.819
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:23.004
Yeah, they're fine.

00:02:23.004 --> 00:02:23.837
They're fine.

00:02:23.837 --> 00:02:24.821
- [Mark] You talk to them?

00:02:24.821 --> 00:02:26.522
- They're with Jose, my husband.

00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:27.543
Sure, yeah.

00:02:27.543 --> 00:02:29.476
When I see them, yeah.

00:02:29.476 --> 00:02:31.798
I don't have no problems with that.

00:02:31.798 --> 00:02:34.312
That's just the way they were born.

00:02:34.312 --> 00:02:35.439
- [Mark] Do you have a phone?

00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:38.772
- Yeah, in Rancho Cucamonga and in Shea-

00:02:40.119 --> 00:02:41.530
- [Mark] No, but do you have a cell phone

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.957
to call your children?

00:02:42.957 --> 00:02:43.875
- A cell phone?

00:02:43.875 --> 00:02:45.728
- [Mark] Do you have a
phone to call your children?

00:02:45.728 --> 00:02:49.362
- Just the one they
handed me back over there,

00:02:49.362 --> 00:02:50.195
where I was at.

00:02:50.195 --> 00:02:52.312
But no and that's okay.

00:02:52.312 --> 00:02:53.554
That's fine.

00:02:53.554 --> 00:02:54.837
Yeah, just the little,

00:02:54.837 --> 00:02:55.802
the different ones

00:02:55.802 --> 00:02:57.454
that I didn't know how to work them

00:02:57.454 --> 00:02:58.618
'cause I wasn't sure what-

00:02:58.618 --> 00:02:59.574
- [Mark] Do your kids know-

00:02:59.574 --> 00:03:01.457
- But I learned how real quick.

00:03:01.457 --> 00:03:03.824
- [Mark] Do your kids know
that you're here on the street?

00:03:03.824 --> 00:03:07.539
- Yeah, they know I'm a good mother.

00:03:07.539 --> 00:03:10.733
My kids were a little bit smarter than me.

00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:13.566
Fell through again, like a turtle.

00:03:14.508 --> 00:03:16.244
But why do I say that?

00:03:16.244 --> 00:03:17.077
Oh, I don't know.

00:03:17.077 --> 00:03:21.283
I saw a turtle in Riverside
or something there,

00:03:21.283 --> 00:03:23.572
but it was more a "Poltergeist".

00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:25.239
That's a nice movie.

00:03:26.627 --> 00:03:28.123
- [Mark] Do you have any problems

00:03:28.123 --> 00:03:29.122
living on the street?

00:03:29.122 --> 00:03:30.473
- [Elizabeth] No, no.

00:03:30.473 --> 00:03:31.306
- [Mark] Nobody hassles you?

00:03:31.306 --> 00:03:33.612
- Nope and nobody,

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:35.336
no bad-mouthing nobody,

00:03:35.336 --> 00:03:38.422
and nobody gave me harassment
not even to gossip.

00:03:38.422 --> 00:03:39.255
- [Mark] They leave you alone?

00:03:39.255 --> 00:03:41.022
- [Elizabeth] They don't
even use words like that.

00:03:41.022 --> 00:03:43.343
Like Hackenberg, a school teacher.

00:03:43.343 --> 00:03:46.154
He was a New York school
teacher, you know?

00:03:46.154 --> 00:03:48.482
'Bout that big, yeah.

00:03:48.482 --> 00:03:51.088
He was from Jay high school.

00:03:51.088 --> 00:03:53.386
The brown book where you study history.

00:03:53.386 --> 00:03:55.415
Yeah, that's how I made my skin.

00:03:55.415 --> 00:03:56.248
My body's like-

00:03:56.248 --> 00:03:57.600
- [Mark] Do you use any

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.891
of the drugs that are out here?

00:03:58.891 --> 00:04:03.002
- [Elizabeth] No, maybe
some of the kill-pains.

00:04:03.002 --> 00:04:03.835
Sure, yeah.

00:04:03.835 --> 00:04:04.866
Anybody would.

00:04:04.866 --> 00:04:06.955
But I was never obnoxious with it.

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:08.806
- [Mark] No alcohol or drugs?

00:04:08.806 --> 00:04:10.628
- [Elizabeth] No.

00:04:10.628 --> 00:04:14.144
Well, in Las Vegas you
couldn't help yourself to that,

00:04:14.144 --> 00:04:15.864
but I never took advantage of that,

00:04:15.864 --> 00:04:17.188
'cause I couldn't.

00:04:17.188 --> 00:04:20.526
But they couldn't even
get it if they tried,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.373
and they were trying

00:04:21.373 --> 00:04:23.706
to get that out in the open.

00:04:25.405 --> 00:04:27.215
Take it out on some, but you know,

00:04:27.215 --> 00:04:28.938
some people like that.

00:04:28.938 --> 00:04:30.176
But not for me.

00:04:30.176 --> 00:04:32.283
- [Mark] How many years have
you lived on the street?

00:04:32.283 --> 00:04:35.686
- [Mark] Oh, since I
been here in Los Angeles.

00:04:35.686 --> 00:04:37.353
Well, probably like,

00:04:38.702 --> 00:04:39.860
two plus one,

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.770
three years I've been here now.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.780
I think.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.455
Yeah, the shelter.

00:04:44.455 --> 00:04:45.757
- [Mark] What were you doing before that?

00:04:45.757 --> 00:04:49.303
- [Elizabeth] Oh nothing,
just married and had kids.

00:04:49.303 --> 00:04:51.712
And then I worked at restaurants.

00:04:51.712 --> 00:04:53.023
I had a good job.

00:04:53.023 --> 00:04:56.604
And no, I didn't make very much money,

00:04:56.604 --> 00:04:59.039
but that was enough to learn.

00:04:59.039 --> 00:04:59.872
- [Mark] What happened to you

00:04:59.872 --> 00:05:01.097
that you ended up homeless?

00:05:01.097 --> 00:05:03.026
- Oh, just the way it was

00:05:03.026 --> 00:05:06.200
just lucky like that, probably.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.685
My family was like that in the past.

00:05:08.685 --> 00:05:11.952
I couldn't figure out
how they did that, so.

00:05:11.952 --> 00:05:14.901
And that's why Pandora, she always,

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:17.068
my cousin, she was always,

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:20.969
faster than me.

00:05:20.969 --> 00:05:22.219
I was too slow.

00:05:23.687 --> 00:05:24.931
She couldn't take it no more.

00:05:24.931 --> 00:05:26.329
She takes it out on me, you know?

00:05:26.329 --> 00:05:29.162
That's the way it was in the past.

00:05:30.777 --> 00:05:32.701
- [Mark] And do you
have parents still, or?

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:35.567
- Yeah, they're still happy.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:36.804
KW and Ken,

00:05:36.804 --> 00:05:38.730
that's what I called them.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.391
When I saw a picture of them though,

00:05:40.391 --> 00:05:42.771
the other day in Los Angeles.

00:05:42.771 --> 00:05:45.053
They were wondering where
they'd been all these years.

00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:47.582
Oh, well they live in Jay, Oklahoma.

00:05:47.582 --> 00:05:50.827
You know, somewhere out in the country,

00:05:50.827 --> 00:05:51.660
that's where they live.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.482
I didn't choose that for them.

00:05:53.482 --> 00:05:58.309
That was their favorite
place to be but I didn't-

00:05:58.309 --> 00:06:02.413
- [Mark] When's the last time
you spoke to your family?

00:06:02.413 --> 00:06:03.246
- Oh, Jay.

00:06:04.336 --> 00:06:05.169
Oh gosh.

00:06:08.432 --> 00:06:10.806
I'm not sure what year that was.

00:06:10.806 --> 00:06:12.889
Cause I've been sleeping.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.747
I sleep a lot, a daily thing,

00:06:16.747 --> 00:06:18.933
but I always wake up and look at the,

00:06:18.933 --> 00:06:20.660
but when's the last time I talked

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.591
to my parents and Jay?

00:06:22.591 --> 00:06:23.591
Oh, let's see.

00:06:23.591 --> 00:06:24.720
She moved down there,

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.182
so it'd be

00:06:26.182 --> 00:06:28.082
about 10 years ago,

00:06:28.082 --> 00:06:29.550
something like that.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.199
- [Mark] And where do you eat?

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:33.008
- Oh, just whatever my mother,

00:06:33.008 --> 00:06:33.841
the eggs.

00:06:33.841 --> 00:06:34.674
I eat bread and butter
- [Mark] I mean

00:06:34.674 --> 00:06:36.225
where do you eat now?

00:06:36.225 --> 00:06:37.502
- Oh, where do I eat now?
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:37.502 --> 00:06:41.705
- The shelter mostly with
my friends and family.

00:06:41.705 --> 00:06:44.553
We're all mixed in, yeah, together.

00:06:44.553 --> 00:06:47.231
- [Mark] Do you have any
friends here on the streets?

00:06:47.231 --> 00:06:49.532
- Well, not strangers, no.

00:06:49.532 --> 00:06:50.918
No, not that I know of.

00:06:50.918 --> 00:06:52.136
I thought of others.

00:06:52.136 --> 00:06:54.261
But I didn't, never.

00:06:54.261 --> 00:06:55.511
No, never ever.

00:06:58.227 --> 00:07:01.460
I always go back to people
that were good to me

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:04.685
because that's just the way it is.

00:07:04.685 --> 00:07:07.660
I remember when I was in school,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.410
I graduate 12th grade

00:07:10.759 --> 00:07:14.035
at Central High School in Tulsa, Oklahoma.

00:07:14.035 --> 00:07:14.868
My friend,

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:17.441
he was a real nice friend,

00:07:17.441 --> 00:07:20.547
he'd sit by me or this
and that or whatever.

00:07:20.547 --> 00:07:23.829
I couldn't remember exactly
what he was thinking,

00:07:23.829 --> 00:07:26.323
but he was right about a lot of things,

00:07:26.323 --> 00:07:29.250
she is something out there.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.700
But yeah, it is nice in Los Angeles

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:36.395
because they bring back
the happy things, you know?

00:07:36.395 --> 00:07:37.228
- [Mark] But what was the happiest

00:07:37.228 --> 00:07:38.434
point of your life?

00:07:38.434 --> 00:07:40.534
- Oh, getting a high school diploma.

00:07:40.534 --> 00:07:42.701
And five times I got that.

00:07:45.154 --> 00:07:48.800
Eighth grade in San
Bernardino High School.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.550
And then I find another
this and that school,

00:07:54.204 --> 00:07:58.287
high school plus the other
school in Los Angeles.

00:07:59.285 --> 00:08:00.800
I didn't know that was there.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:04.852
I was so surprised, I couldn't believe it.

00:08:04.852 --> 00:08:07.523
And it was so lucky to have school anyways

00:08:07.523 --> 00:08:10.106
because they were so into that.

00:08:11.284 --> 00:08:13.368
- [Mark] Elizabeth, have
you ever been treated

00:08:13.368 --> 00:08:16.323
for any mental conditions
or anything like that?

00:08:16.323 --> 00:08:19.922
- Yeah, schizophrenia with Dr. Schlechter.

00:08:19.922 --> 00:08:21.470
I like him.

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:22.960
Yeah, I do.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.127
I already had that answered in my body

00:08:28.546 --> 00:08:33.039
and I didn't know what to
do with and he knows it.

00:08:33.039 --> 00:08:34.740
- [Mark] And do you take
the medications for that?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.348
- Yeah. I take a lot of 'em.

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:38.095
Especially when it's looking right at you

00:08:38.095 --> 00:08:38.928
and you know-

00:08:38.928 --> 00:08:42.150
- [Mark] Are you taking them now?

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.904
- No, just a little bit of pills I take.

00:08:44.904 --> 00:08:46.237
but I never take

00:08:48.698 --> 00:08:50.249
OD on anything

00:08:50.249 --> 00:08:51.856
because I'm not like that.

00:08:51.856 --> 00:08:54.870
You can't make somebody
be what you want to be.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.154
- [Mark] But living on the street,

00:08:56.154 --> 00:08:56.987
I'm guessing that maybe

00:08:56.987 --> 00:08:58.711
you're not taking your medications?

00:08:58.711 --> 00:08:59.544
- Oh yeah.

00:08:59.544 --> 00:09:01.580
Yeah, I take some pills.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.070
Pain or things that control your mind,

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:07.704
just like exercise every day.

00:09:07.704 --> 00:09:10.747
But if you don't want
to eat or you're full,

00:09:10.747 --> 00:09:13.241
then you'll get skinny again.

00:09:13.241 --> 00:09:16.186
It all depends upon how you look at it

00:09:16.186 --> 00:09:18.769
when you saw your arms and lap.

00:09:19.739 --> 00:09:23.054
But I don't know what the hell for.

00:09:23.054 --> 00:09:23.887
I never-

00:09:23.887 --> 00:09:24.720
- [Mark] All right, Elizabeth.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.743
- I never thought of that.

00:09:25.743 --> 00:09:26.576
- [Mark] Well, Elizabeth.

00:09:26.576 --> 00:09:28.147
Thank you for talking with me.

00:09:28.147 --> 00:09:29.244
- You're welcome.

00:09:29.244 --> 00:09:31.089
- [Mark] And I wish you the best

00:09:31.089 --> 00:09:32.983
of luck living on the street like this.

00:09:32.983 --> 00:09:35.808
- Yeah, that is something.

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:37.470
- [Mark] It seems like you should

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.197
probably be taken care
of somehow, in some way.

00:09:41.197 --> 00:09:44.146
- Yeah, I'm just looking at myself.

00:09:44.146 --> 00:09:46.579
Isn't that something?

00:09:46.579 --> 00:09:47.889
The body.

00:09:47.889 --> 00:09:49.361
I think that dirt could be,
- [Mark] When's the last time

00:09:49.361 --> 00:09:50.915
you took a shower?

00:09:50.915 --> 00:09:52.636
- I didn't say dirt, huh?

00:09:52.636 --> 00:09:54.143
- [Mark] When's the last
time you took a shower?

00:09:54.143 --> 00:09:55.976
- Oh, when my mascara.

00:09:57.071 --> 00:09:58.358
Oh, when I took a shower?

00:09:58.358 --> 00:09:59.573
- [Mark] When was the last
time you took a shower?

00:09:59.573 --> 00:10:01.990
- Oh, over there by 7-Eleven.

00:10:02.919 --> 00:10:04.615
Yeah, that's the place I take a shower.

00:10:04.615 --> 00:10:07.110
Over on sixth street.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:08.028
They had showers.

00:10:08.028 --> 00:10:09.003
The cold one-

00:10:09.003 --> 00:10:10.797
- [Mark] But when's the
last time you took one?

00:10:10.797 --> 00:10:14.011
- Oh, about two or three days ago.

00:10:14.011 --> 00:10:14.898
(Elizabeth sniffing)

00:10:14.898 --> 00:10:16.864
Yeah, I'm fine, I smell beautiful.

00:10:16.864 --> 00:10:20.281
But I always find these beautiful things.

00:10:21.237 --> 00:10:23.239
I couldn't believe it how nice it was.

00:10:23.239 --> 00:10:24.072
I was thinking,

00:10:24.072 --> 00:10:26.098
my God, who gave me all these things?

00:10:26.098 --> 00:10:28.398
I didn't even know that.

00:10:28.398 --> 00:10:30.337
Didn't know it.

00:10:30.337 --> 00:10:31.542
- [Mark] All right, Elizabeth.

